## Frequently asked questions

### Do I need a US-based agency to grow in the US?

No. Search engines do not rank a site higher because its consultant is American. What matters is a clear US version of your site, US keyword research and US signals that are true. A US-based team can help with local PR and US links. The structure, hreflang and US pages can be planned and run from the UK.

### Should my US pages sit on a .com or a .co.uk?

A .com with a /us/ folder is usually the simplest choice if you own it. A .co.uk is tied to the UK in Google's eyes. US pages on it can struggle. Moving domains is a migration. I check the risk with you before recommending it.

